<div style="width: 100%; padding: 20px; background-color: #f0f8ff; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; border: 2px solid #1a5276;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; padding: 5px; font-size: 2.2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # My Multilingual Self – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em; font-style: italic;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> My Multilingual Self</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> The Benefits of Multilingualism</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Demonstrate comprehension of extended discussions on abstract topics. Interactive: Describe the storyline of an audio or visual narrative.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can demonstrate comprehension of an extended discussion on multilingualism in Panama's service sector (e.g., "The speaker said that being bilingual is essential for engineers working on international infrastructure projects, as they need to communicate with foreign clients and partners." "Another point mentioned was that multilingualism in logistics companies operating in the Panama Canal Zone improves coordination with global stakeholders, opening doors to higher-level management positions.")
Can describe the storyline of an audio narrative about a bilingual person in Panama, noting how multilingualism was helpful (e.g., "In the story, the shop owner said that speaking both Spanish and English helped attract more tourists.")
Can summarize an audio segment on multilingual education in Panama, highlighting challenges and solutions (e.g., "The speaker said that students in Bocas del Toro benefit from practicing English with tourists, even though access to formal language courses can be limited.")</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f5f5f5;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher begins by projecting images of people speaking different languages in various contexts (e.g., a tour guide, a scientist at an international conference, a market vendor). Students are asked to briefly discuss in pairs what they observe and what benefits they think multilingualism might offer in these situations. The teacher elicits initial ideas using prompts like, "What advantages do these people have?" or "How might being multilingual help them succeed (/s/) in their careers?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary words from the curriculum, focusing on word stress in "multilingualism," "multicultural," and "language learning." The teacher also highlights the pronunciation of /s/ in "success" and /z/ in "citizens." Sentences demonstrating target grammar (Reported speech, Future simple, Modals of ability) are introduced: "She said that multilingualism opens many doors," "Companies will prioritize hiring bilingual employees," "You can communicate effectively with diverse clients."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If someone is 'proficient' in a language, do they speak it perfectly or just a little bit?" (Expected answer: Perfectly / Very well.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'companies will prioritize hiring bilingual employees,' does that mean they will hire them first or last?" (Expected answer: First.)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 7-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Multilingual Self".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> An authentic audio segment (approx. 2-3 minutes) from a local Panamanian podcast featuring an interview with a young professional discussing their multilingual journey and how it has enhanced their career opportunities in the service sector (e.g., tourism, logistics, or international business in Panama). The audio includes examples of reported speech (e.g., "She said that having a high level of language proficiency was necessary for her role"), future simple for predictions (e.g., "I believe that businesses will continue to prioritize employees who can communicate effectively"), and modals of ability (e.g., "You can easily excel in a multicultural environment here"). The audio content will naturally introduce the target vocabulary: *multilingualism, language, proficiency, communication, career, opportunities, business, education, fluency, skill, bilingual, effective, international, diverse, multicultural, necessary, fluent*.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening comprehension for understanding the main ideas and specific details of extended discussions on abstract topics related to multilingualism.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>First Listen (Gist):</b> Students listen once and choose the best main idea from a set of 3 options (e.g., "a) The challenges of learning new languages, b) The importance of multilingualism for career growth in Panama, c) How to travel without speaking local languages").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Second Listen (Details):</b> Students listen again and complete a True/False exercise or match statements to the speaker's specific points. For example:
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 4px; margin-bottom: 0;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The speaker said that being bilingual is essential for engineers working on international infrastructure projects." (True/False)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Multilingualism in logistics companies operating in the Panama Canal Zone improves coordination with global stakeholders." (True/False)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The speaker believes that learning languages can enhance personal communication skills." (True/False)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Identifying and understanding specific details, opinions, predictions, and abilities mentioned in the audio using reported speech, future simple, and modals of ability. Focusing on target vocabulary related to *multilingualism, proficiency, communication, career, opportunities, business, education, fluency, skill*.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Gap-Fill Listening (Controlled Practice):</b> Students receive a transcript of a key segment of the audio with gaps for 8-10 target vocabulary words (e.g., *proficiency, opportunities, communicate, business, excel, enhance*). They listen to the audio a third time and fill in the missing words. Teacher checks answers by replaying specific parts of the audio or having students volunteer answers.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Opinion Reporting (Semi-controlled):</b> Students are given a worksheet with prompts like "The speaker said that..." or "The interviewer asked if companies will..." They listen to specific sentences from the audio again and complete the prompts, paraphrasing the speaker's opinions or predictions using reported speech and future simple. (e.g., "The speaker *said that* global stakeholders *will* coordinate better with multilingual logistics companies.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Ability Identification (Pair Check):</b> Students work in pairs. They listen to the audio segment one last time, specifically noting examples of what a multilingual person *can* or *cannot* do according to the speaker. They then share their findings, using modal verbs of ability, e.g., "He mentioned that you *can* connect with different cultures," or "She *argued* that one *can* achieve higher-level management positions." This reinforces the pronunciation of /z/ in "citizens" as they discuss interacting with diverse citizens.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 12-15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Multilingual Self".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Discussion and Summary Sharing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> In small groups of three, students discuss the audio segment. Their task is to collaboratively summarize the key benefits of multilingualism in Panama's service sector, as presented by the speaker, and describe a specific anecdote or example mentioned in the audio. They must use at least three pieces of reported speech and two instances of future simple or modals of ability. They should also incorporate at least five of the target vocabulary words (e.g., *career, opportunities, communication, proficiency, diverse*). They should aim to promote cultural inclusiveness in their discussion, as described in the pragmatic competence, acknowledging and supporting diverse language learning backgrounds in their group.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example prompt for groups:</b> "Based on the podcast, what did the speaker *say* are the main benefits of being multilingual in Panama? What *will* companies look for in the future? What *can* multilingual people achieve? Describe an anecdote from the audio."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in discussing comprehension of the audio, collaborative interaction, and communicative task completion through summarizing and describing while embedding target grammar and vocabulary. Emphasize discussing language diversity, promoting cultural inclusiveness, and offering culturally sensitive advice.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group discussions, focusing on listening comprehension demonstrated through accurate summarization and the use of target language. Peer assessment will also be used where students evaluate their group members' contributions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group orally presents a 1-minute summary of their discussion, highlighting the main points from the audio and incorporating their descriptions. They should demonstrate comprehension of the extended discussion and describe an anecdote from the audio.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Demonstrated comprehension of the audio's main points (Learning Outcome: Can demonstrate comprehension of an extended discussion).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of the summary/description.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of reported speech, future simple, and modals of ability.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of at least five target vocabulary words (e.g., *multilingualism, career, proficiency, communication, opportunities*).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation, particularly of target words and sounds (/s/, /z/, word stress).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative interaction and contribution within the group.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Name one new thing you learned about the benefits of multilingualism from today's audio."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which new vocabulary word from today's lesson will you try to use this week?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 6-8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did listening to the audio help you understand the importance of multilingualism in Panama?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the listening activity did you find most challenging, and how did you overcome it?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well in this lesson to enhance students' listening comprehension? Were the vocabulary introduction and grammar points sufficiently practiced through the listening tasks? What adjustments or scaffolds might be needed for students who struggled with the pace or complexity of the audio? (e.g., pre-teaching more vocabulary, providing a glossary, using visual aids for abstract concepts). Ensure that the connection to next lesson provides a smooth transition to Reading Comprehension.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2, students will encounter a written text related to "The Benefits of Multilingualism" in Panama. The vocabulary words introduced and practiced in this listening lesson will reappear in the reading, allowing students to reinforce their understanding and apply their knowledge in a new skill context.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Date: ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Time: 2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>